-<help format="markdown">
-SmartTile prepares and post-processes point-cloud predictions for the 3Dtrees workflow. Select one task according to the stage of processing you want to run.
+    <help><![CDATA[
+**What it does**
+
+SmartTile splits point clouds into tiles for segmentation and species models, puts the predicted tiles back together and transfers the predictions onto the original files. Inputs must use a projected CRS in metres.
+
+- **Tile and subsample**: buffered spatial tiles at up to three voxel sizes or the original resolution, or tiles in which every existing tree stays whole. Also writes a tile bounds JSON and a preview image.
+- **Filter / merge segmented tiles**: removes the buffer overlap between segmented tiles and joins trees cut by tile borders. The remap target transfers the predictions onto finer subsampled tiles first, writes the original files with the predictions like Remap, or is none (filter at the segmented voxel size). RayCloudTools tree tables and meshes are filtered together with the tiles.
+- **Remap predictions to originals**: copies the predicted dimensions of one or more prediction collections onto the original files. Every original point must be covered.
+- **Create merged file**: joins several prediction sets of the same originals into one LAZ, COPC LAZ or PLY file.
 
-**Tile and subsample**
+**Segmentation**
 
-Splits one or more LAZ/LAS point clouds into buffered spatial tiles and writes two subsampled collections. The tile task also writes a tiling preview image and a tile bounds JSON file. Use the tile bounds JSON with the merge task so SmartTile can identify tile cores and buffers consistently.
+.. image:: $PATH_TO_IMAGES/smarttile_segmentation.png
+   :width: 100%
 
-**Filter/Merge segmented tiles**
+Tile the originals at 10 cm for the model and at 1 cm as high-resolution targets. Merge the segmented tiles with the tile bounds JSON, then remap them onto the originals. For a single model without species prediction, **Remap target → Original files** writes the originals directly.
 
-Filters predictions back to tile cores, optionally matches instances across neighboring tiles, optionally reassigns small clusters, and writes merged target-resolution tiles. Provide the segmented prediction files, the target-resolution subsampled files, and the tile bounds JSON from the matching tiling run. If 3dtrees_raycloudtools tree sidecar files are supplied, SmartTile filters and returns those text files while keeping tile-local instance IDs; cross-tile matching and small-cluster reassignment are disabled for that mode.
+**Species per tree**
 
-When original LAZ/LAS files are provided, the merge task can also transfer predictions back to the originals and create prod-merged products.
+.. image:: $PATH_TO_IMAGES/smarttile_whole_instances.png
+   :width: 80%
 
-**Remap predictions to originals**
+Tile originals that already carry tree IDs with **Keep existing instances whole**, run the species model, and remap with **Match within the same existing instance**.
 
-Transfers prediction dimensions from either one merged prediction file or one or more segmented prediction collections back onto the original uploaded LAZ/LAS files. Use the dimension allowlist only when you want to copy a selected set of prediction dimensions from segmented collections.
+**Several models in one file**
 
-**Create prod-merged file**
+.. image:: $PATH_TO_IMAGES/smarttile_merged_file.png
+   :width: 40%
 
-Creates delivery-ready products from original-with-prediction files that already contain prediction dimensions. Prod-merged outputs can be LAZ, COPC LAZ, or binary PLY. COPC LAZ is selected with the format value `copc.laz` and is returned to Galaxy as `laz`; PLY is returned as `plybinary`.
-</help>
+Remap each model separately, then add each result as a **Collection** of **Create merged file**. For ForestStructure, choose full resolution, COPC LAZ and **Add OriginalPointIndex**.
+    ]]></help>
